    expert: 'Minimizes Internal Covariate Shift: calculates mini-batch mean $\\mu_B$ and variance $\\sigma_B^2$: $\\hat{x}_i = \\frac{x_i - \\mu_B}{\\sqrt{\\sigma_B^2 + \\epsilon}}$, followed by learnable scale and shift: $y_i = \\gamma \\hat{x}_i + \\beta$. Smooths the loss landscape.',
    math: 'μ_B = (1/m) Σ x_i,  σ_B² = (1/m) Σ (x_i - μ_B)²\nx̂_i = (x_i - μ_B) / √(σ_B² + ε),  y_i = γ · x̂_i + β\nRunning stats: E[x] ← (1-m)E[x] + m·μ_B',
    descIn: 'Unnormalized raw convolved values with varying dynamic ranges.',
